WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.340
I can’t pledge allegiance to a flag that has no allegiance to me.

2
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.540
It’s pretty much that simple.

3
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:27.260
I can’t say that I support a government that doesn’t support me in all of my freedoms as an American-born woman; not as a black woman.

4
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.260
As an American woman.

5
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:49.200
My oldest record . . . my oldest ancestor on record is sitting at Georgetown University, and she arrived in the United States in 1704.

6
00:00:49.200 --> 00:01:04.440
I ought not to be having any conversations with anybody about my Americanness and my rights as an American.

7
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:10.220
It was, they say, the law of the land.

8
00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:15.240
Okay, it was a bad law then and it’s a bad law now,

9
00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:27.880
and the excuse that it was the law does not negate the damage of the law.

10
00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:33.580
That just gives people a pass.

11
00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:34.980
I’m not passing nobody.
